# NCBI dbGaP analysis accession:	pha004496
# Name:	COPD-Primary
# Description:	Genome-wide association meta-analysis. Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) affection status (binary) was the outcome of interest with case status defined using pre-bronchodilator spirometry values. Cases had forced expiratory volume in 1 second (FEV1)   80% and FEV1/FVC > 0.7.
# Method:	Logistic regression was performed in individual cohorts, checked for orientation and hg19 chr and positions. Summary statistics for each cohort were further assessed using EasyQC. Then, a fixed-effects meta-analysis was performed using METAL.  Analysis includes subjects with both genome-wide and custom genotyping.
# Human genome build:	38
# dbSNP build:	141

# SNP ID:	Marker accession
